# Semgrep scope for the CI `semgrep` job (specs/security/ci-semgrep-scan.md REQ-4).
# Without this file Semgrep applies its built-in default list, which also skips
# every test/ and tests/ directory. This file is that built-in list, copied from
# Semgrep 1.167.0's binary, with only its "Common test paths" block removed
# (test/, tests/, testsuite/, *_test.go), so test code is scanned too.

# Administrative folder or file used by popular version control systems
.git
.svn
_darcs
# Paths to files and folders that are typically large and ignorable
build/
vendor/
dist/
*.min.js
.env/
.tox/
# Package managers
node_modules/
.npm/
.yarn/
.venv/
_opam/
_build/
_cargo/

# A deliberately poisoned fixture: gitleaks MUST trip on its credential-shaped
# strings (REQ-A8, AC-A8.1), so Semgrep's p/secrets would too. Excluded by exact
# path only; nothing else under tests/ is excluded.
